ower BI Developer & Data Analyst

Position Summary
We are seeking a Power BI Developer & Data Analyst to support the design, development, and maintenance of business intelligence solutions. This role will be responsible for building and optimizing datasets, designing Power BI reports and dashboards, and ensuring data structures support accurate and scalable reporting. The ideal candidate has strong analytical skills, experience working with complex data models, and the ability to communicate effectively with business stakeholders.

Key Responsibilities
•⁠  ⁠Design, build, and maintain datasets and data models for Power BI reporting.
•⁠  ⁠Develop interactive Power BI dashboards and reports that support business decision-making.
•⁠  ⁠Analyze and understand data structures, relationships, and business requirements.
•⁠  ⁠Create and optimize data tables, measures, calculations, and KPIs.
•⁠  ⁠Validate data accuracy and troubleshoot reporting issues.
•⁠  ⁠Collaborate with the team leader and teammates to gather requirements and translate them into reporting solutions.
•⁠  ⁠Document data models, reporting logic, and development standards.
•⁠  ⁠Recommend improvements to data architecture and reporting performance.

Qualifications
•⁠  ⁠Minimum 3 years of experience developing Power BI reports and dashboards.
•⁠  ⁠Strong understanding of data modeling, relational databases, data tables, and data structures.
•⁠  ⁠Experience with Power Query, DAX, and data transformation techniques.
•⁠  ⁠Ability to work with large datasets and optimize report performance.
•⁠  ⁠Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.
•⁠  ⁠Fluent English communication skills, both written and verbal.
•⁠  ⁠Ability to work East Coast (U.S.) business hours.
•⁠  ⁠Experience working with distributed or nearshore teams preferred.

Preferred Qualifications
•⁠  ⁠Experience with SQL and data warehousing concepts.
•⁠  ⁠Experience connecting Power BI to multiple data sources (e.g., SQL Server, Snowflake, Databricks, APIs, Excel).
•⁠  ⁠Familiarity with data governance and reporting best practices.